roberts@gaul.csd.uwo.ca (Eric Roberts) writes:

>I am playing hack on a MIPS using a modem and vt100 emulation, when
>a character throws something, however, I get a bunch of garbage on
>the screen... It appears that the emulation can't handle the movement.
>I tried vt220, vt320, vt102, ansi, etc... and nothing works! What emulation
>should I use, or is there something wrong with the terminal programm
>(I use kermit)? When I set ansi, it won't even run but says that the
>term must backspace or something like that.

The problem you are seeing is due to padding characters that
are listed in termcap/terminfo being displayed literally on
the screen, rather than being interpreted normally as padding.

Most likely, nethack was compiled with the "#define TERMINFO"
definition on your system when it should have been compiled without
it.  The only way to correct it is to recompile with the TERMINFO
definition off.  

